{
  "description": "One box mesh placed four times. A parent names a child with a core::child reference, and composing writes a glTF node per relation, so a node named by two parents is written twice. Here two placements share one box, a pair holds both placements, and two rows each hold the pair: 2 rows x 2 placements = 4 boxes, from a single mesh and a single copy of the geometry. A node can only name a given child once, since component names are unique within a node, so placing something twice means two parents.",
